TEST DESIGN TECHNIQUE 
    1. EQUIVALANCE PARTITIONING -
                      - Input data divide into groups (equivalance classes / paritions)
            application -> 18-60
                        - invalid-> less than 18
                        - vlaid -> 18-60
                        - invalid -> greater than 60
          ADV->
              - reduce number of test case 
              - save testing time 
              - good test coverages
        DIS->
            - boundary value may be missed

2. BOUNDARY VALUE ANALYSIS ->
                  - it focuses on testing the boundary of valid  and invalid input ranges 
            application-> can cast vote - 18-70
                - Developers cna often make mistakes as 
                    1. using"<" instead of "<="
                    2. using ">" instead of ">=" 
        - in such cases using the equivalance partitioning may not reaveal the defects 
    BOUNDARY VALUE ANALYSIS (BVA)
                        - below minumun (17)
                        - just minimum (18) 
                        - above mminimum (19)
                        - below maximun (69)
                        - just maximum (70)
                        - above maximum(71)

